xecution; repository discovery outside the two tagged source files and the supplied benchmark inputs.\n\n## Affected areas\n\n§ 6.1\nFuture implementation target: button-chain.html, with a named body DOM subtree for initial markup, a named appendButton() interaction function, a named handleButtonActivation() completion branch, and a .completion-message style token. Plan-only artifacts include the UI story, cache, verification companions, review, bug register, trackers, context snapshot, validation, and analysis report.\n\n## Constraints and decisions\n\n§ 7.1\nThis is an isolated planning proof for revision 1.3.1. Only the tagged repository-local skill and its relative UI reference may guide the plan. No HTML artifact or execution tooling may be created or used. The browser target is deliberately a future local file route-discovery method, recorded as unexecuted because the benchmark forbids browser execution.\n\n## Risks and open questions\n\n§ 8.1\nThe future executor must confirm the exact generated-button labeling and whether “fourth generated button” counts the first appended button as generated; this plan records the acceptance interpretation as the fourth appended button and requires the executor to resolve any product clarification before implementation. Browser evidence is unavailable in this proof by explicit benchmark constraint.\n\n## UI classification\n\n- UI affected: yes\n- Rationale: <why>\n\n## UI validation\n\n- Required: yes\n- Browser target: No browser execution permitted; future local file route discovery for button-chain.html\n- Story artifact: `ui-user-stories.md`\n\n## Adversarial review\n\n- Artifact: `adversarial-review.md`\n- Status: 💤 pending\n===== basic-test-proof-1.3.1-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan/ui-user-stories.md\n# UI user stories: basic-test-proof-1.3.1-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan\n\n| ID | Persona / precondition | Browser actions | Interaction evidence | Expected observable result | Status | Evidence | Related work units | Run cache |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| US-01 | A visitor opening the future local button-chain.html file in a fresh browser context | Open the future local file route, confirm one button, click the current last button four times in order, and observe the completion state. | Mouse click on the rendered current last button for each activation. | The initial view has one button; each of the first three clicks adds exactly one button below the prior last button; the fourth generated button clears the document and leaves exact lowercase text finished with a visible white border. | 💤 untested | — | W01,W02,W03,W04,W05 | `ui-story-runs/US-01.md` |\n===== basic-test-proof-1.3.1-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan/bugs.md\n# UI bugs: basic-test-proof-1.3.1-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan\n\n| ID | Story | Severity | Reproduction/evidence | Investigation goal | Fix goal | Retest story | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n===== basic-test-proof-1.3.1-20260810T121526Z-benchmark8-isolated-plan/ui-story-runs/US-01.md\n# Browser run cache: US-01\n\n## Starting state\n\n- Fresh browser context at the future local file route for button-chain.html; one visible initial button; no prior generated buttons.\n\n## Buffered interaction sequence\n\n| Order | Direct UI input | Target / value | Expected readiness signal |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Mouse click the rendered current last button, repeated in order for four activations. | Current last button, then the newly appended current last button, four total clicks | After each click the button count or completion text visibly changes; after the fourth click only finished remains with a visible white border. |\n\n## Waits and readiness\n\n| After order | Wait or condition | Maximum wait | Observed result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | After each click the button count or completion text visibly changes; after the fourth click only finished remains with a visible white border. | 2 seconds per readiness condition | Not run yet |\n\n## Run result\n\n- Status: `💤 untested`\n- Evidence: Pending browser run.\n- Cache validity: Created for the current planned interaction sequence.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
