igger incorrectly. The task says to press the fourth generated button. Starting from the initial button, clicks 1–4 generate buttons 1–4; button 4 is then pressed on click 5. The draft instead says the fourth activation clears the document, and its acceptance/story/cache assert only three appends followed by completion. | Rewrite W03, its testing companion, the UI story, cache, coverage, goal handoffs, and all dependent wording so clicks 1–4 each append exactly one button and click 5 presses generated button 4 and then clears the document. Record the observable counts/targets at each checkpoint. | ❌ unresolved |\n| AR-03 | The append verification does not prove the required fourth generated button exists: W02 verifies only three clicks and W03 starts from an unspecified “fourth visible generated-button state.” The final W05 flow also has only four clicks. | Make the append test verify four sequential appends and a five-click completion flow. Define the starting state and exact current-last target after every click; make the completion test explicitly press generated button 4, not merely perform a fourth activation. | ❌ unresolved |\n| AR-04 | The UI run cache is not a faithful executable cache: one row compresses four clicks into “repeated in order,” omits the separate four append checkpoints and the fifth completion click, and gives one readiness condition for the whole sequence. | Replace the cache with one ordered row per direct mouse click (five total), naming the target/value and readiness signal after each click, including button counts 2, 3, 4, and 5 after appends and the final `finished`/border state after completion. Update the story to reference that exact sequence. | ❌ unresolved |\n| AR-05 | `plan-description.md` contains unresolved template text (`Rationale: <why>`) and still marks the adversarial review pending. The inventory decomposition checklist is also entirely unchecked despite the draft claiming a complete decomposition. | Replace the placeholder with the concrete UI rationale, update the plan review status only after this independent artifact is approved, and mark each decomposition checkbox only after the corrected inventory/step one-to-one mapping is verified. | ❌ unresolved |\n| AR-06 | The plan leaves a material requirement ambiguity in “fourth generated button” and tells the future executor to resolve it, even though the supplied task contract is precise enough to establish the sequence. That makes the handoff non-deterministic. | Remove the open question and state the exact interpretation: initial button is not generated; the first four appended buttons are generated buttons 1–4; pressing generated button 4 is the completion action. Keep any implementation detail separate from this fixed acceptance contract. | ❌ unresolved |\n| AR-07 | The named implementation symbols (`appendButton()`, `handleButtonActivation()`, and `.completion-message`) are presented as required change targets without distinguishing chosen design from confirmed existing symbols; no HTML exists in this proof. This can force an executor to invent an API or split a single inline implementation incorrectly. | Either explicitly designate these as the planned symbols/tokens to create in `button-chain.html` and describe their ownership/connection, or use a bounded discovery/design work unit before implementation. In either case, state the event binding, generated-button counter, and completion element/style contract in one executable handoff. | ❌ unresolved |\n| AR-08 | The bug-recovery path is referenced only procedurally in a testing companion. The empty `bugs.md` does not state the required severe/non-severe recovery linkage or the retest dependency for this story, so a future failure can be recorded without a complete plan path. | Add a concrete bug-feedback section to the plan or story artifacts stating that a failed US-01 becomes `🐛 bug found`, gets a `bugs.md` row with reproduction/evidence, investigation goal, fix goal, and retest story, and that the story is rerun after the fix; preserve the benchmark’s prohibition on running it during this proof. | ❌ unresolved |\n\n## Verdict\n\n- Status: `❌ rejected`\n- Rationale: The draft is not executable against the exact requested behavior: its completion sequence is off by one generated button and its browser cache/tests cannot prove the required interaction. Mandatory durable artifacts and review/decomposition evidence are also missing, with unresolved placeholders and a non-deterministic handoff. The plan must be revised and independently reviewed again before approval.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
